{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "04 A mind is born",
  "description": "A native mind from creation to its first model call: the create route, the row and token, the workspace, start through the supervisor and its driver, the optional OS sandbox, the hub connection, and the first call through the hive's model gateway. Lines were read at this repository's handover commit; if a line has moved, search the file for the step's function or symbol name.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "hive/core/app.py",
      "line": 1239,
      "title": "1. POST /api/agents",
      "description": "A person (or the local operator) creates a mind. Asking for extra tools needs an admin. Naming a swarm needs sight of that swarm. The creator becomes the owner; visibility defaults to private (tour 06)."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/hive.py",
      "line": 742,
      "title": "2. Hive.create_agent",
      "description": "The new mind's lock and its swarm's membership fence are taken before the row is visible, and held until the setup in `finish_agent` is done. Insertion into a swarm checks, in the same statement, that the swarm is still open."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/hive.py",
      "line": 755,
      "title": "3. The row and its token",
      "description": "Checks name and kind, refuses joining someone's personal swarm, applies role defaults and validates tools. A random token is created; only its hash is stored. A new mind starts as `created` with desired state `stopped`, on the hive's default driver."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/hive.py",
      "line": 789,
      "title": "4. finish_agent",
      "description": "Grants the mind publish rights in its swarm's commons (tour 02), asks the supervisor to prepare a workspace, writes the body description (`placement.write_body`), applies the role, and announces the mind on the live stream."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/supervisor/workspace.py",
      "line": 167,
      "title": "5. The workspace",
      "description": "A native mind gets its own folder: `run.metta`, links to the OmegaClaw core and the ChromaDB library, a `token` file readable only by its owner (0600), its prompt and its tools. An external member (`module`) gets an empty folder only: it runs elsewhere and just uses its token."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/app.py",
      "line": 1315,
      "title": "6. Start (or wake)",
      "description": "`/api/agents/{id}/start`, `stop`, `sleep` and `wake` all go to `Hive.lifecycle` (`hive/core/hive.py` line 1078), which serialises everything for one mind under its lock. External members cannot be started here; they connect with their token."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/hive.py",
      "line": 1124,
      "title": "7. _start_locked",
      "description": "Marks the mind `starting`, desired `awake`, in one statement that also checks the swarm is not archived (so it cannot race an archive). Then it calls `supervisor.start` (line 1143)."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/supervisor/drivers.py",
      "line": 521,
      "title": "8. Supervisor.start",
      "description": "Every start moves the mind's generation first; the hub uses it as an admission fence for connections. The driver is chosen per mind (`local` or `docker`). The start also records whether a genuinely new process began, which the Ask uses as a context boundary."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/supervisor/workspace.py",
      "line": 221,
      "title": "9. The mind's environment",
      "description": "What the mind is told: the hub socket URL and its token, the agent API URL, and the model route at `<hive>/llm/v1` with the mind's own token as the API key. The mind never sees a provider key. `Supervisor.env` (`hive/supervisor/drivers.py` line 493) adds a launch id."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/supervisor/drivers.py",
      "line": 172,
      "title": "10. LocalDriver.start",
      "description": "The process gets an **allowlisted** environment only, never the hive's own (keys, secrets, settings). With `HIVE_MIND_SANDBOX=1` the hive refuses to start without an OS sandbox and wraps the command. The process runs in its own session, so its whole group can be stopped. Sandboxing is opt-in: deployments set it, development does not (`STATUS.md`)."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/supervisor/sandbox.py",
      "line": 53,
      "title": "11. The sandbox wrap",
      "description": "On macOS, a `sandbox-exec` profile; on Linux, a Landlock profile applied by `landlock.py` before the command runs. The profile is written to disk so it can be inspected. With neither available, starting a sandboxed mind is refused."
    },
    {
      "file": "modules/channel_hive/src/hive_channel.py",
      "line": 595,
      "title": "12. The mind dials the hub",
      "description": "Inside the mind, the hive channel connects to `/agent-hub` with its bearer token and sends `resume` with the last sequence it saw, so nothing queued is lost or delivered twice."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/app.py",
      "line": 2017,
      "title": "13. The hub accepts the connection",
      "description": "The token is checked. `admit_connection` refuses a mind that is stopped or asleep, so a late connection never wakes it. After the accept, `agent_connected` (`hive/core/hive.py` line 1454) re-checks the fence and registers the socket. Then the loop handles `resume` (replay), acks and `agent_message` frames."
    },
    {
      "file": "lib_llm_ext.py",
      "line": 289,
      "title": "14. The mind's model provider is the hive",
      "description": "The OmegaClaw core registers a provider named `Hive` that points at the hive's `/llm/v1` route and uses the mind's hive token. The hive picks the real model and supplies the key."
    },
    {
      "file": "hive/core/app.py",
      "line": 2063,
      "title": "15. The first model call",
      "description": "`/llm/v1/chat/completions` authenticates the mind, estimates the worst-case cost, checks budgets, reserves the money, calls the provider through the gateway and records usage. Tour 05 walks this route step by step."
    }
  ]
}
